= Internal power struggle

Our currents are fighting for the control over the party. Which way should we support?

Left - Supports revolutionary course, reconciliation with KPD and class war against bourgeiouisie.

Center - Supports middle course, insisting that the conditions of revolution must come.

Labor - Pragmatic unionists, advocating for uncompromissive stance on rights of workers.

Reformist - Pragmatic reformists, advocating for the governance to push forward socialist policies and eventual transition of economy.

[? if neorevisionism: Neorevisionism - Supports the militant republicanism to save the republic from the claws of extremism and seeks to limit it by any means given. ?]

- @left
- @center
- @labor
- @reformist
- @neorevisionist
- @root: Leave.
- @easy_discard

@left
title: Support the **Left**.
subtitle: Revolutionary course is the only way.
on-arrival: left_strength += 9; left_dissent -= 5; radicalization += 1; democratization += 1; reformist_strength -= 5; reformist_dissent += 5; labor_dissent += 5; neorevisionist_dissent += 7

We have supported the leftist course, for bourgeouisie is the main threat. Reformists, laborites [? if neorevisionism: and neorevisionists ?] are mad at our decision to support the leftists.

@center
title: Support the **Center**.
subtitle: The middle course demands patience.
on-arrival: center_strength += 9; center_dissent -= 5; left_strength -= 5; left_dissent += 3; reformist_dissent += 3; labor_dissent += 3; neorevisionist_dissent += 3

We have supported the centrist course, insisting that revolution cannot be rushed. Leftists, reformists, laborites [? if neorevisionism: and neorevisionists ?] are mad at our decision to support the centrists.

@labor
title: Support **Labor**.
subtitle: The workers' rights come first.
on-arrival: labor_strength += 9; labor_dissent -= 5; left_dissent -= 2; center_strength -= 5; center_dissent += 5; left_dissent += 5

We have supported the labor unionists, for the rights of workers cannot wait. Centrists and leftists are mad at our decision to support the laborites.

@reformist
title: Support the **Reformists**.
subtitle: Gradual transition through governance.
on-arrival: reformist_strength += 9; reformist_dissent -= 5; democratization += 1; left_strength -= 5; left_dissent += 5; center_dissent += 5; neorevisionist_dissent -= 2

We have supported the reformist course, trusting governance to carry socialism forward step by step. Leftists and centrists are mad at our decision to support the reformists.

@neorevisionist
title: Support the **Neorevisionists**.
subtitle: The republic must be saved from all extremes.
view-if: neorevisionism
on-arrival: neorevisionist_strength += 9; neorevisionist_dissent -= 5; democratization += 2; radicalization -= 1; left_strength -= 5; left_dissent += 7; center_dissent += 5

We have supported the neorevisionist course, favoring militant republicanism over any extreme. Leftists and centrists are mad at our decision to support the neorevisionists.

@root
title: Leave.

We have chosen not to intervene in the internal struggle, for now.
